---
description: Accessibility standards following WCAG 2.2 AA.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Accessibility

Accessibility is mandatory.

Never treat accessibility as optional.

---

# Standard

Follow WCAG 2.2 AA.

---

# Semantic HTML

Always use semantic elements.

Examples:

header

main

section

article

nav

footer

button

label

---

# Keyboard Navigation

Every interactive element

must be reachable using Tab.

Visible focus states are required.

---

# Buttons

Buttons must:

Have accessible names.

Be keyboard accessible.

Have sufficient touch targets.

---

# Forms

Every input:

Requires a label.

Use proper validation messages.

Associate errors correctly.

---

# Images

Every informative image

must include meaningful alt text.

Decorative images

should use empty alt attributes.

---

# Color

Never rely solely on color

to communicate meaning.

---

# Contrast

Meet WCAG AA contrast ratios.

---

# Motion

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

Provide non-animated alternatives where appropriate.

---

# Screen Readers

Use ARIA only when semantic HTML is insufficient.

Avoid unnecessary ARIA attributes.

---

# Goal

Every user should be able to use the application independently.